we've talked some about the meaning of  the cards but now I want to show you how  they use for fortune-telling I'm going  to shuffle the deck and then I'm going  to lay them out in one of the most  common patterns the Celtic cross  normally we would be doing a reading for  a specific person in this case I don't  have someone to do a reading for so I'm  just going to talk about what the cards  would mean in different positions the  first card is intended to represent the  person who is asking the question the  current this card is laid in the center  upright or reversed however it's drawn  from the deck and then another card is  played across that this card represents  the problems that the person is facing  in this case our first card was the  three of swords which you can tell it's  somewhat a bleak card to begin with and  then it's been crossed with the tower  and the tower as we mentioned before  it's quite a difficult card you can see  that it's a bit of chaos either upright  or reversed to the left of these cards  we place one that represents the past of  the person in question and to the right  we place a card that represents their  future above we place a card that  represents the conscious goals of our  current below we place one that  represents their subconscious goals you  can see a lot of duality here the self  and the conflict the before and the  after the conscious and the subconscious  after that four cards are stacked from  bottom to top on the right hand side the  first one represents advice that should  be given to the current the second one  is about external influences which could  be positive or negative  card number nine second-to-last  represents the hopes and fears of the  current this is one card where it's  especially important to look at both the  regular meaning and the reversed  meanings finally our last card card  number ten is about the outcome that is  likely to occur this outcome card can  also be read both reversed and upright  you can think of it as if you take the  advice this will happen if you don't  take the advice that will happen this  requires a lot of work between the  fortune teller and the current you need  to understand the meaning of the cards  but you also need to understand where  that person is when they're asking the  question you can't just do a reading  blank for someone you need to know a  little bit about them so that's one of  the most important things to know about  all of this  you can't automatically generate this  just because someone takes the advice  that was prescribed for them doesn't  mean that they are going to be free with  their money or that they're going to be  covetous of it you need to understand  where that person is in their life and  what the appropriate advice to give is  based on that card you can't just read  it straight and hope that it works  this is common across a lot of  fortune-telling systems including Aoife  in the Yoruba tradition you really need  a connection with a human being so this  is the Celtic Cross it's not the only  spread that you'll see people will  arrange cards in different ways  especially with different decks but it  is the most common and if you go to a  fortune-teller you might see them use  this spread
 

